pyramid Capability Maturity of a Platform Engineering Organisation

// stress: many-items — twelve tiers, each with a two-line description

Autonomous purple
  Teams ship without platform tickets.
  Guardrails enforce policy automatically.

Predictive blue
  Capacity and cost forecast ahead of demand.
  Incidents are caught before customers notice.

Optimised cyan
  Golden paths cover most new services.
  Unit economics are tracked per team.

Measured green
  DORA metrics are reported quarterly.
  Error budgets drive release decisions.

Governed yellow
  Security reviews are part of the pipeline.
  Every service has a named owner.

Self-service orange
  Environments are created from a catalogue.
  Access is requested and granted in minutes.

Automated red
  Builds, tests and deploys run on every merge.
  Infrastructure is declared in code.

Standardised purple
  One language per layer, one pipeline template.
  Shared libraries replace copied code.

Documented blue
  Runbooks exist for the top ten failure modes.
  Architecture diagrams are kept in the repo.

Visible cyan
  Logs, metrics and traces reach one place.
  Alerts page a person, not a channel.

Repeatable green
  Releases follow the same steps each time.
  Rollbacks have been rehearsed once.

Ad hoc yellow
  Each team builds and ships its own way.
  Knowledge lives in a few heads.
